> Know something, I've never recieved an artifact from a god. Do you
> have to make your god EXTREMELY happy first, or is there a special
> procedure, or am I still just unlucky?

Altar of your own alignment (could have been converted).  Fresh
corpse (so don't bother with zombies and such), prayer timeout
already zero (so avoid praying whenever possible as in eat corpses
so you don't have to use prayer to cure weak-level hunger).  #offer.

Those are the basics.  Then it becomes a mamter of the odds.
Folks new to altars tend to think in numbers of sacrafices that have
too few digits.  The chances of the first gift are in the 1-in-10s and
as your horde of artifacts increases it rapidly grows to 1-in-100s.

Either you haven't known what the requirements are or you haven't
done nearly enough sacraficing.  It's *way* too easy to pray every
time you're week and never get an artifact because you're doing that.
Or to decline to convert altars or whatever.



